3,Niger-Congo Language Family - Structure & Writing - MustGo,https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/niger-congo-language-family/,"The earliest evidence of a Niger-Congo language dates back to Portuguese records of the 16th century. However, few grammars were published prior to the 19th century although the first known grammar of an African language (Kongo) was written by an Italian missionary in 1659.","Maninkakan, Western",Niger-Congo
